     How each replacement was chosen. The move is proportional to how wrong the colour
     was, because two of the seventeen are not obviously wrong at all. "Master Thief"
     wore hue 5, saturation 1, lightness 12 — a near-black with a whisker of tan in it,
     which reads as dyed leather rather than as a leg — so it moved one saturation rung
     to the grey rung, keeping its hue and its lightness exactly, and the value it moved
     to is one his own palette already carried. "Alexander" wore hue 6, saturation 6,
     lightness 20, a dark oxblood, and moved one rung the other way, to the fully
     saturated rung the derivation calls a costume colour rather than a complexion —
     again the same hue and the same lightness. Repainting either of those any further
     would have been a regression in appearance rather than a repair.

     The rest are mid or light tans where the leg genuinely reads as bare, and they move
     into a family the figure is already wearing: brown and khaki for the farm and
     monastery records, neutral grey for the pale ones, blue-grey for a fisherman.
     Nothing became a colour the character would not wear.

     Where they moved TO is worth one paragraph, because six of the seventeen landed on
     hue 8 — 8472 three times, 8481 twice, 8613 once — and hue 8 is the rung immediately
     outside the gamut being escaped. CitizenEcho.isFlesh's own javadoc names that rung
     as the one place the rule knowingly cuts skin: 30 of the game's 3,320 face recolours
     target hue 8, and one of them, 8646, is the skin base's own saturation and lightness
     one rung along.

     None of the six is that colour or near it. 8472 is hue 8, saturation 2, lightness
     24 and renders #3F3821 — a very dark olive-brown, forty-six lightness rungs below
     the complexion the javadoc worries about, and nobody would read it as a leg. So the
     objection is narrower than "these are still skin-coloured", and it is not nothing:
     there was no reason to step one rung over the line when hue-0 greys were available
     and were used for six other records in the same table. The rung was chosen to keep
     each figure in a colour family it was already wearing, which is the sentence above,
     and the six are named here so that a reader deciding how much slack the gamut has
     is not told the repaints landed further from it than they did.

     Sixteen of the seventeen replacements are values the dataset already carried
